<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hada Chauhans</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hadas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hadas are a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> clan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajputs</a>, who ruled the region of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadoti">Hadoti</a> after them. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rao-deva">Rao Deva</a> took Bundi in 1342, and a junior line founded the separate state of Kota in the 17th century. Hada rulers served as Mughal commanders and later governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> under British paramountcy until they joined independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
